if you're like me and you didn't manage  to swipe an early copy of no man's sky  then you still might be wondering what  exactly you will be doing in this space  faring exploration game in a blog post  Shaun Murray has detailed some of the  things you will be doing in order to  manage expectations and clarify the  nature of the game according to the blog  post some of the things you will  definitely be doing are exploring a  universe of procedurally generated  worlds with beautiful creatures trading  with NPCs combat against robots mechs  and cool space battles and surviving and  crafting in a universe size sandbox if  you're expecting a game where you could  pilot freighters engage in PvP combat  and build civilizations no man's sky is  not the game you've been waiting for but  Murray goes on to say that these things  could be coming in future updates if  you've heard anything about no man skies  first update and you probably know that  this update alone is adding a loft you  can check out a detailed list on  gamespot but beware of spoilers Murray  concluded the blog post by saying this  game is not for everyone it's a weird  game it's a niche game and it's a very  very chill game no man's sky launches  for ps4 on August ninth and for PC on  August twelfth for more on no man's sky  make sure to keep those spaceships doc  dick gamespot
 

